<newsitem itemid="208027" id="root" date="1996-11-21" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: ED&amp;F Man raises H1 payout, sees strong yr.</title>
<headline>ED&amp;F Man raises H1 payout, sees strong yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.9		    vs 8.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.4		    vs 3.2</p>
<p> Pretax		     27.2		   vs 32.8</p>
<p> Trading profit	   121.6		  vs 117.4</p>
<p> Operating profit	 34.4		   vs 42.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Commodities and financial services company E D &amp; F Man said it had remained confident of reaching a satisfactory outcome for the year as a whole and had accordingly raised its interim dividend by 6.0 percent despite some profit slippage.  </p>
<p> Associates income	0.9		    vs 0.7 loss</p>
<p> Interest paid	    9.0		    vs 7.3</p>
<p> Tax			  8.1		    vs 10.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		  19.1		   vs 22.6</p>
<p> Attributable	     17.9		   vs 21.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 7, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Dec 10</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Dec 2</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
